Spec: TemplateMod

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Sub-command dispatcher for `agent template …`: owns the private `tenant`, `service`
    and `system` leaf modules — the offline Helm-less templating lane (render package
    manifests locally) — plus the shared @Contexts enum their leaves embed.

Owns:
  ./mod.rs

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap `Parser`, `Debug`; single field @command: @Commands. Consumed by
    ./../main.rs (`Template` dispatch arm; spec pending ./../main.sdd).
  @Commands — clap `Subcommand`, `Debug`, exactly three variants with `///` doc help
    verbatim: @Tenant(tenant::Parameters) doc `Template a tenant package`,
    @Service(service::Parameters) doc `Template a service package`,
    @System(system::Parameters) doc `Template a system package`.
  @Contexts — clap @ValueEnum, @Default (`@Simple` arm carries `#[default]`),
    @Debug, @Clone, serde @Serialize + @Deserialize; arms exactly: @Simple doc
    `Minimal context`, @HA doc `High-availibity context` — the misspelling in that
    doc string is frozen (never rename without a contract review; help output shows
    it verbatim).

Accepts:
  A parsed @Commands tree; leaf flag contracts in ./tenant.sdd, ./service.sdd,
    ./system.sdd.

Returns:
  `()` — @run is NOT async (unlike the system/service/tenant/boxes dispatchers);
    success falls off the end, @Err lanes end in @std::process::exit.

Handles:
  Leaf @Err (leaves are sync): Tenant `Templating a tenant package failed with: {e:}`
    → exit 1; Service `Templating a service package failed with: {e:}` → exit 1;
    System `Templating a system package failed with: {e:}` → exit 3.
  Panics inside leaves — unwound; main's #[tokio::main] runtime is still alive because
    template::run is called synchronously from the async main body.

Must:
  Keep `mod service; mod system; mod tenant;` private and re-export nothing but the
    items listed under Exposes (@Contexts is the only symbol other leaves import as
    `super::Contexts`).
  Call NO @common::context::init_k8s(): this is the one dispatcher with no kube
    client dependency at the dispatch level; leaf need is frozen per their specs.
  Keep @HA doc-string typo `High-availibity` byte-exact.
  Return from @run without any @await — the three leaf @run calls are synchronous.

Depends on:
  ./tenant.sdd, ./service.sdd, ./system.sdd — leaf contracts (each embeds @Contexts
    via its @Parameters).
  ./../main.rs — caller (`template::run(args)`, no await); spec pending ./../main.sdd.

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide later whether `High-availibity` is corrected (help-text-only change,
      but frozen until reviewed) and whether @Contexts serde derives need a stable
      wire representation (lowercase? today serde defaults to "Simple"/"HA").
  [ ] Decide the tenant/system exit-code story (1 vs 3 mirrors system-mod's install
      vs delete split with no operator consumer documented).
  [ ] Cover the dispatcher with tests; none exist in this file.

Done when:
  Dispatch, @Contexts shape/defaults/typo, and the sync-no-k8s posture hold under
    tests.

Scenario: contexts enum defaults to Simple
  Given `TemplateMod` @Contexts
  When @Default::default is called
  Then @Simple is returned and clap renders `Minimal context` in help
  And @HA still renders its frozen `High-availibity context` typo

Scenario: system templating failure exits 3
  Given @Commands::System whose sync leaf returns @Err
  When @run reaches the system arm
  Then the frozen system log line prints and @process::exit(3) is reached
